# DTF tier manifest: dos
# Profile-set: filesystem / single, with the login rate-limiter ENABLED.
# This is the ONLY tier that flips the shipped control ON so it is actually
# tested: today's k8s gate overlay runs with RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false, which is
# why the rate-limit / worker-starvation DoS classes (matrix row 9) go untested.
# DTF's base already defaults RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true; this manifest sets it
# EXPLICITLY so the intent is unmistakable and a future base change cannot
# silently disable the control this tier exists to gate.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (A) login-limiter HOLDS — repeated failed logins get 429 after the threshold
#       (with the control OFF, no 429 ever appears -> the assertion FAILS).
#   (B) worker-starvation is BOUNDED — a capped burst on the bcrypt/auth CPU path
#       does not wedge availability (/health stays live, backend recovers, no
#       genuine 5xx fault). The load is deliberately capped: a test, not a DoS.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="true"
